[thin] The specified 2.0 mm spring leaves and R1.5 root transitions provide the intermediate section Derek requests between the physically tested 1.3 and 2.6 mm leaves. These are the flexures, printed on an axial end so bending lies in the layer plane. Repeated insertion and bending distribution are physical checks on the complete pointed samples.
alternatives: Thickening the leaves to 2.6 mm repeats the section Derek reports bending only at its corners; 1.3 mm repeats the thinner section he requests an intermediate value above. The broad central bearing stock is independent of these spring lengths.
