[thin] The deliberately pointed free edge joins the single planar lead-in to the outside spring wall. Derek requests this point as the production tip. Its thickness approaches zero at the edge; the working spring remains 2 mm and the continuous solid retaining nose remains 1.6 mm. These locations are on that specified point.
alternatives: A flat tip land removes the requested point. Thickening the full leaf changes the selected flexure section rather than the lead-in. The point is integral with the cap.
